# xyml — Extended YAML Module

**Location:** `src/yasched/utilizing/xyml/`

xyml (Extended YAML) is a superset of YAML that allows composing a complete
YAML document from multiple files. When the parser encounters a mapping that
contains a **directive key** (a special string such as `__file__` or `__ext__`),
it loads the referenced file, processes it recursively, and splices its content
into the document at that point.

Directive keys are registered at startup in a singleton registry. Third-party
code can register additional keys with custom behaviours.

Class diagram: *(see individual design docs below)*

---

## File map

```
src/yasched/utilizing/xyml/
  __init__.py
  XymlKeyBehavior.py       # enum: REPLACE | EXTEND
  XymlKeyRegistry.py       # singleton registry of directive keys
  XymlLoader.py            # recursive loader — public entry point
```

